# _headers — the deployment's security headers, ARTIFACT-ENFORCED.
#
# Next copies public/ into the static export verbatim, so this file ships
# inside out/ and the host (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify _headers convention)
# applies it at the edge. It replaces the deleted middleware.ts (per-request
# CSP nonce) and next.config headers() — both incompatible with
# `output: 'export'`. Policy provenance: git history of those two files.
#
# Static-export adaptations, deliberate:
#   - script-src: 'unsafe-inline' in place of the former per-request nonce
#     (no server to mint one). Hash-pinning the inlined bootstrap scripts at
#     build time is the future hardening; 'wasm-unsafe-eval' stays for
#     @react-pdf's fontkit (Harfbuzz WASM, the /audit evidence-bundle PDF).
#   - connect-src: scheme-wide https:/wss:/ws: + loopback. A wallet points
#     this frontend at its OWN RPC + IPFS endpoints (/settings — the
#     composition cost model), so the endpoint set is the USER'S, not
#     enumerable here. https: also covers XMTP's :5558 gRPC-web ports.
#   - img-src loopback: the local Kubo gateway (127.0.0.1:8080) serves
#     catalogue/branding pins on a devnet.
#   - font-src data:: fontkit loads its WASM as a data: URI; fonts.gstatic
#     kept from the former policy.
#   - worker-src blob:: @react-pdf's layout worker.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: http://127.0.0.1:* http://localhost:*; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' data: ws: wss: https: http://127.0.0.1:* http://localhost:*; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://*.walletconnect.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(self)
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# /evidence-display is iframed by arbitration-forum reviewers. The ancestor
# list is deployment CONFIG (the dispute layer is provider-agnostic): a
# deployment that recognizes a forum EDITS this frame-ancestors line (e.g.
# 'self' https://resolve.kleros.io). The unconfigured default admits no
# third-party ancestor. X-Frame-Options is detached so the legacy header
# can't override the CSP allowlist.
#
# Two matcher blocks, same policy: trailingSlash: true exports the route as
# `evidence-display/index.html`, served at `/evidence-display/` — hosts match
# `_headers` paths literally, so both the slashless and the directory form
# are pinned. A deployment editing the frame-ancestors list edits BOTH lines.
/evidence-display
  ! X-Frame-Options
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: http://127.0.0.1:* http://localhost:*; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' data: ws: wss: https: http://127.0.0.1:* http://localhost:*; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://*.walletconnect.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

/evidence-display/*
  ! X-Frame-Options
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: http://127.0.0.1:* http://localhost:*; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' data: ws: wss: https: http://127.0.0.1:* http://localhost:*; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://*.walletconnect.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
